  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q73-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve $\\log_2(x-1)=2\\log_2(x+1)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No solution.\n\nThe power property gives $x^2+x+2=0$, whose discriminant is $-7$.",
      "worked": "The original domain requires $x-1>0$ and $x+1>0$, hence $x>1$. The power property is valid on this domain.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(x-1)&=\\log_2\\big((x+1)^2\\big)\\\\x-1&=(x+1)^2\\\\x^2+x+2&=0\\\\\\Delta&=1^2-4(1)(2)\\\\\\Delta&=-7\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe discriminant is negative, so there are no real roots. Therefore the logarithmic equation has no solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
